ef="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>’s coup destroys the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omride-dynasty">House of Omri</a>; Jehu pays tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 788–747 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeroboam-ii">Jeroboam II</a>, Israel’s last period of prosperity</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">732 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-iii">Tiglath-pileser III</a> annexes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilead">Gilead</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">722 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> falls to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> after a long siege</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">720 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> deports some 27,000 people and creates the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samerina">Samerina</a></span></li></ol>
